WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.284 --> 00:00:01.117
(plodding music)

00:00:01.117 --> 00:00:01.950
- Okay.

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:03.213
(doorbell rings)

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:04.750
- Hi.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.163
- Have you heard the
story of Joseph Smith?

00:00:06.163 --> 00:00:07.688
(door slams)

00:00:07.688 --> 00:00:08.521
(doorbell rings)

00:00:08.521 --> 00:00:09.391
- Start with Jesus.

00:00:09.391 --> 00:00:10.224
- Okay.

00:00:10.224 --> 00:00:11.892
- Everybody likes Jesus.

00:00:11.892 --> 00:00:13.449
What we meant to say was, do you...

00:00:13.449 --> 00:00:15.165
(door slams)

00:00:15.165 --> 00:00:17.209
I think that a lot of
people think it's so easy to

00:00:17.209 --> 00:00:18.814
be religious.

00:00:18.814 --> 00:00:19.647
- Good morning.

00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:20.480
- Care to talk about Jesus Christ?

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.313
- How are you doing?
- No, I'm in a hurry.

00:00:21.313 --> 00:00:22.146
- Oh, no worries.
- Goodbye.

00:00:22.146 --> 00:00:22.979
- Hey, how ya' doing?

00:00:22.979 --> 00:00:25.478
- Do you believe in Jesus Christ?

00:00:25.478 --> 00:00:26.311
- Aw.
- That's okay.

00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:28.978
- Okay, good luck.
- Not at all?

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.384
- How are you all doing this morning?

00:00:34.384 --> 00:00:36.857
- What are you girls up to today?

00:00:36.857 --> 00:00:38.648
- In my six months of being
a missionary for the Church

00:00:38.648 --> 00:00:40.980
of Jesus Christ of Latter
Day Saints, my faith has been

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.715
tested all the time.

00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:44.826
- So we actually don't smoke,
that's part of our church.

00:00:44.826 --> 00:00:46.894
We don't smoke and we don't drink and...

00:00:46.894 --> 00:00:48.258
- That's why Mormons are the best looking.

00:00:48.258 --> 00:00:49.091
- Yeah.

00:00:50.696 --> 00:00:51.529
- Ah,

00:00:51.529 --> 00:00:54.587
Don't look to your right,
there's a big ol' sign,

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.420
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.253
- Just don't even bother.

00:00:56.253 --> 00:00:57.086
I told you not to look there.

00:00:57.086 --> 00:00:57.919
- Oh my gosh.

00:00:57.919 --> 00:01:01.019
- I do want to help people,
people just don't seem to

00:01:01.019 --> 00:01:02.112
always want to be helped.

00:01:02.112 --> 00:01:03.466
Oh, hi there, how you doing?

00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:04.673
- Enormous, check this out!

00:01:04.673 --> 00:01:05.520
(screaming)

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.367
- Would you like to know
about the one true church?

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:10.200
- Are you serious?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.606
- Do you want to know
about my (beep) instead?

00:01:11.606 --> 00:01:12.439
Come here, come here.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.301
- This is dangerous, stop it.

00:01:13.301 --> 00:01:14.736
Run, run.

00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:16.325
- You know I miss my mom
and dad, and I miss my three

00:01:16.325 --> 00:01:18.159
older brothers, Mark, Jared and Brian.

00:01:18.159 --> 00:01:20.633
And my three younger
brothers, Luke, Paul and Gary.

00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:22.398
However, despite all this,
at the end of these two

00:01:22.398 --> 00:01:25.239
years, at least I have my
gal Linda to come home to.

00:01:25.239 --> 00:01:27.962
- Did you propose before you left?

00:01:27.962 --> 00:01:30.678
- No, I was gonna wait
until the mission was done.

00:01:30.678 --> 00:01:34.348
And after I got into
dental school and stuff.

00:01:34.348 --> 00:01:35.860
- Right.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.427
- What do you mean, right?

00:01:38.427 --> 00:01:39.681
- Nothing.

00:01:39.681 --> 00:01:42.984
I had a girl back in Vegas
but Heavenly Father had

00:01:42.984 --> 00:01:47.151
another plan for her and she
married a returning missionary.

00:01:48.485 --> 00:01:52.748
I've been on my mission here
in Los Angeles for almost

00:01:52.748 --> 00:01:54.538
two years since then.

00:01:54.538 --> 00:01:57.404
I only have a couple of months left.

00:01:57.404 --> 00:02:00.237
And I don't really want it to end.

00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:03.171
- Ezra's in there.

00:02:03.171 --> 00:02:06.170
(piano music)

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.778
(screaming)

00:02:07.778 --> 00:02:09.323
- Ow, ow, ow!

00:02:09.323 --> 00:02:11.578
- Do you feel the spirit now? (laughs)

00:02:11.578 --> 00:02:12.874
- Ow, why'd you do that?

00:02:12.874 --> 00:02:15.374
- For me, faith is like
music, you just have to follow

00:02:15.374 --> 00:02:18.076
the beat and also be a good singer.

00:02:18.076 --> 00:02:20.419
If you're not a good
singer, you could play the

00:02:20.419 --> 00:02:21.546
tamborine or something.

00:02:21.546 --> 00:02:24.331
Or just be quiet and
listen to the Holy Spirit.

00:02:24.331 --> 00:02:26.642
(knocking)

00:02:26.642 --> 00:02:28.362
- Hi there, have you heard
about the restoration

00:02:28.362 --> 00:02:29.195
of the Gospel?

00:02:29.195 --> 00:02:30.433
(door slams)

00:02:30.433 --> 00:02:32.522
(knocking)

00:02:32.522 --> 00:02:34.082
- Good morning, Sir.

00:02:34.082 --> 00:02:35.944
We're just gonna leave a
pamphlet under your door if you

00:02:35.944 --> 00:02:38.194
don't mind, thanks so much.

00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:41.666
(knocking)

00:02:41.666 --> 00:02:43.262
- [In Unison] Hello.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:44.501
(door slams)

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.794
- Must be a little breezy, you
got use a little more muscle,

00:02:46.794 --> 00:02:48.009
there you go.

00:02:48.009 --> 00:02:49.012
- Whoa.

00:02:49.012 --> 00:02:50.688
You know, something might be
wrong, let's try the top of

00:02:50.688 --> 00:02:52.039
the...there we go.

00:02:52.039 --> 00:02:54.289
(whispers)

00:02:55.146 --> 00:02:55.979
There.

00:02:57.086 --> 00:02:59.024
I know we should find an
investigator, but I really don't

00:02:59.024 --> 00:03:01.300
want another door in my face.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.464
- Maybe we shouldn't lead with
Joseph Smith is a prophet.

00:03:05.464 --> 00:03:06.532
- What do you lead with if
you don't lead with Joseph

00:03:06.532 --> 00:03:07.632
Smith is a prophet?

00:03:07.632 --> 00:03:08.550
Like that's the best part.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:09.383
(doorbell rings)

00:03:09.383 --> 00:03:10.468
- Coming.

00:03:10.468 --> 00:03:11.989
Hello?

00:03:11.989 --> 00:03:13.109
- Hi, we're from the Church
of Jesus Christ of Latter

00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:13.942
Day Saints.

00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:14.948
- Are you a Star Wars fan?

00:03:14.948 --> 00:03:15.781
- Star Wars?

00:03:15.781 --> 00:03:16.614
No.

00:03:16.614 --> 00:03:18.285
Not really, why?

00:03:18.285 --> 00:03:19.597
- What about a Britney Spears fan?

00:03:19.597 --> 00:03:20.500
- Who doesn't like Britney?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.763
- What if the Old Testament
is like Baby One More Time

00:03:23.763 --> 00:03:26.429
and the New Testament
is Oops I Did It Again,

00:03:26.429 --> 00:03:28.554
the Book of Mormon is Britney.

00:03:28.554 --> 00:03:30.042
- Oh, I'm a Slave For You, Britney.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:30.901
- Yes.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.601
When it's finally about the dance.

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:34.014
Do you mind if we come in and
talk about the Book of Mormon?

00:03:34.014 --> 00:03:34.847
This is great.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:35.680
- Uh, sure.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:36.672
- Hi I'm Elder Alan.

00:03:36.672 --> 00:03:38.553
- So you guys are Christian, right?

00:03:38.553 --> 00:03:40.198
- Yeah, it's in the name,
the Church of Jesus Christ of

00:03:40.198 --> 00:03:41.400
Latter Day Saints.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.847
- What makes you any different
from all the other churches

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:43.818
out there?

00:03:43.818 --> 00:03:45.520
- We don't drink alcohol.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.295
- Okay, I haven't drank
for about a month now, so.

00:03:48.295 --> 00:03:49.825
- Hey, that's awesome.

00:03:49.825 --> 00:03:52.964
- I feel fresh, I feel rejuvenated.

00:03:52.964 --> 00:03:54.643
- We also don't use tobacco.

00:03:54.643 --> 00:03:56.858
- Well I smoke but I'm trying to cut back.

00:03:56.858 --> 00:03:58.782
- Self improvement is so important.

00:03:58.782 --> 00:03:59.886
- And then it's just no caffeine.

00:03:59.886 --> 00:04:01.203
- No caffeine?

00:04:01.203 --> 00:04:02.617
So how do you wake up in the morning?

00:04:02.617 --> 00:04:05.266
- Well, as it says in the
doctrine and covenants,

00:04:05.266 --> 00:04:06.392
you know we're not really supposed to.

00:04:06.392 --> 00:04:07.225
- What?

00:04:07.225 --> 00:04:08.058
In what?

00:04:08.058 --> 00:04:10.416
- Well it's kind of like
the liner notes on an album.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.380
- So there's these words of
wisdom that say there are

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.143
these certain harmful substances that we

00:04:14.143 --> 00:04:15.265
should abstain from.

00:04:15.265 --> 00:04:17.437
- (stutters) It, it's
even in the New Testament.

00:04:17.437 --> 00:04:19.878
"Know ye not that ye are
a temple of God and that

00:04:19.878 --> 00:04:22.483
the spirit of God dwelleth in you?"

00:04:22.483 --> 00:04:24.487
- Okay, so my body's like a temple.

00:04:24.487 --> 00:04:25.510
I like that.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:27.856
What's your stance on the LGBT community?

00:04:27.856 --> 00:04:29.291
- What's an LGBT?

00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:30.426
- The gay people.

00:04:30.426 --> 00:04:32.116
- Why would you want to know about that?

00:04:32.116 --> 00:04:34.587
- Why do you listen to
so much Britney, then?

00:04:34.587 --> 00:04:36.349
- I like to dance.

00:04:36.349 --> 00:04:37.932
- Yeah, I like men.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.414
- Oh, dang.

00:04:41.414 --> 00:04:44.311
(door slams)

00:04:44.311 --> 00:04:46.655
- I hope I didn't send him
any mixed signals or anything.

00:04:46.655 --> 00:04:48.189
I touched his hand.

00:04:48.189 --> 00:04:49.606
- Hey Mormons, check this out!

00:04:49.606 --> 00:04:51.007
(screaming)

00:04:51.007 --> 00:04:51.840
- I can't see.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:52.673
Zack, I can't see.

00:04:52.673 --> 00:04:53.506
I can't see.

00:04:53.506 --> 00:04:54.666
- We should teach her.

00:04:54.666 --> 00:04:56.578
- I can't see, I can't see.

00:04:56.578 --> 00:04:57.689
- Oh no, oh no.

00:04:57.689 --> 00:04:58.606
- I got it.

00:04:59.469 --> 00:05:02.048
- I mean there's gonna
be more losses than wins,

00:05:02.048 --> 00:05:04.457
that's just how this thing works, but...

00:05:04.457 --> 00:05:06.024
I'm sorry, I just think

00:05:06.024 --> 00:05:06.857
(crying)

00:05:06.857 --> 00:05:09.668
it's been really hard this week.

00:05:09.668 --> 00:05:13.106
I miss my mom and dad
and I miss my brothers

00:05:13.106 --> 00:05:16.682
and I miss my girlfriend
and I don't know what

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:18.058
I'm doing.

00:05:18.058 --> 00:05:19.713
I want the spirit to help me do better.

00:05:19.713 --> 00:05:21.670
I just don't think I'm doing it.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.606
I don't really want to do this anymore.

00:05:23.606 --> 00:05:25.773
(sobbing)

00:05:28.293 --> 00:05:29.126
- Hey Ezra?

00:05:29.126 --> 00:05:29.959
- Yeah.

00:05:29.959 --> 00:05:30.959
- It's Zack.

00:05:31.817 --> 00:05:34.285
Hey buddy, you trying to
get out of sight and out of

00:05:34.285 --> 00:05:35.286
sound of me?

00:05:35.286 --> 00:05:36.119
- No.

00:05:36.119 --> 00:05:38.895
(laughs)

00:05:38.895 --> 00:05:42.255
It's tough being away
from your family, I know.

00:05:42.255 --> 00:05:44.098
It was tough for me when I first got here.

00:05:44.098 --> 00:05:47.098
You gotta hold on to your testimony.

00:05:48.521 --> 00:05:49.776
- I know.

00:05:49.776 --> 00:05:52.051
- That's what will keep you strong.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.662
You know what helps you
hold on to your testimony

00:05:53.662 --> 00:05:55.412
better than anything?

00:05:57.469 --> 00:05:58.969
Singing about God.

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:03.046
Hey Boggs, get your
guitar, come on in here.

00:06:03.046 --> 00:06:06.546
(sentimental piano music)

00:06:13.817 --> 00:06:16.851
- That's how it is, right,
just when you're out of faith,

00:06:16.851 --> 00:06:19.601
that's when your friends show up.

00:06:20.563 --> 00:06:23.980
I'm gonna keep spreading the word of God.

00:06:26.909 --> 00:06:29.891
♫ Joseph Smith

00:06:29.891 --> 00:06:32.141
(laughter)

00:06:33.859 --> 00:06:35.357
Thanks guys.

00:06:35.357 --> 00:06:36.774
- You're welcome.

00:06:38.058 --> 00:06:40.145
- How you doing, Boggs?

00:06:40.145 --> 00:06:42.062
- Um, my dad just died.

00:06:44.615 --> 00:06:45.948
Wanna sing more?

00:06:47.537 --> 00:06:48.370
- Yeah.

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:49.203
- Sure.

00:06:49.203 --> 00:06:51.806
(guitar music)

00:06:51.806 --> 00:06:54.560
♫ We will walk

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.643
(funky upbeat music)

